			"date": "2022-11-30T22:15:32.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://social.vivaldi.net/@michaelklein\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>michaelklein</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I did something similar for a bit. </p><p>Stage 1, seeing if Mastodon suited me:<br>Crosspost my tweets to here. </p><p>Stage 2, happy here. Leave breadcrumbs:<br>Switch to crossposting toots to twitter. </p><p>Stage 3, giving up on twitter:<br>Remove crossposting and get comfy here.</p><p>Feeling pretty at ease going quiet over there now, and just participating in what feels like a much more constructive environment here.</p>",
